export const SIGN_INFO: SignInfo[] = [{"n": "aries", "dates": "Mar 21 - Apr 19", "el": "Fire", "mod": "Cardinal", "ruler": "Mars", "traits": "bold, direct, energetic, competitive", "love": "Aries loves chase and honesty. They bring passion early and need a partner who can keep pace.", "work": "Natural starters who do best with clear goals and room to lead.", "card": "The Emperor", "cardSlug": "the-emperor", "strengths": "Aries energy is at its best when it has somewhere honest to go. Courage, directness and the willingness to go first are rare gifts, and people lean on Aries in a crisis precisely because Aries does not freeze. The blind spot is the flip side: impatience, a short fuse, and starting more than gets finished. Growth for Aries is learning that slowing down is not the same as losing.", "growth": "A simple practice for Aries: before acting on a strong impulse, name it out loud and wait one full day. The impulses that survive the wait are usually the right ones. In relationships, Aries does well to ask before charging ahead on a partner's behalf.", "tarot": "In tarot, Aries is traditionally linked to The Emperor, the card of structure, authority and self-rule. The pairing is a reminder that Aries fire works best when it builds something that lasts."}, {"n": "taurus", "dates": "Apr 20 - May 20", "el": "Earth", "mod": "Fixed", "ruler": "Venus", "traits": "steady, loyal, sensual, stubborn", "love": "Taurus loves slowly and fully. Loyalty and comfort matter more than grand gestures.", "work": "Patient builders who value stability, craft and reliable income.", "card": "The Hierophant", "cardSlug": "the-hierophant", "strengths": "Taurus energy builds the things other signs only talk about: savings, gardens, recipes, relationships that last decades. Patience and follow-through are the quiet superpowers here. The blind spot is rigidity: staying too long in a job, a home or an argument because leaving feels like waste. Growth for Taurus is learning that changing course is not the same as quitting.", "growth": "A simple practice for Taurus: once a season, change one small routine on purpose and notice that nothing breaks. In relationships, Taurus does well to say 'I need' out loud instead of expecting a partner to notice.", "tarot": "In tarot, Taurus is traditionally linked to The Hierophant, the card of tradition, craft and what gets passed down. The pairing honors Taurus as the keeper of what is worth keeping."}, {"n": "gemini", "dates": "May 21 - Jun 20", "el": "Air", "mod": "Mutable", "ruler": "Mercury", "traits": "curious, quick, witty, restless", "love": "Gemini needs conversation first. A partner who keeps them mentally interested keeps them close.", "work": "Fast learners who thrive in communication, variety and ideas.", "card": "The Lovers", "cardSlug": "the-lovers", "strengths": "Gemini energy connects: ideas, people, jokes, fields that never met before. Curiosity and adaptability make Gemini the person who can talk to anyone in the room. The blind spot is scatter: ten tabs open, three projects alive, and a reputation for vanishing when things get repetitive. Growth for Gemini is learning that depth and variety can coexist.", "growth": "A simple practice for Gemini: finish one small thing every week before starting the next, and keep a single list instead of five. In relationships, Gemini does well to say when they need space rather than simply fading.", "tarot": "In tarot, Gemini is traditionally linked to The Lovers, the card of choice, duality and honest communication. The pairing reflects Gemini's lifelong work of choosing, and choosing again, with eyes open."}, {"n": "cancer", "dates": "Jun 21 - Jul 22", "el": "Water", "mod": "Cardinal", "ruler": "Moon", "traits": "caring, intuitive, protective, moody", "love": "Cancer loves through care and memory. Emotional safety is the foundation of everything.", "work": "Nurturers who excel where trust, care and intuition count.", "card": "The Chariot", "cardSlug": "the-chariot", "strengths": "Cancer energy makes places feel like home. Memory, loyalty and emotional radar let Cancer notice what others miss: the friend who went quiet, the mood in a room. The blind spot is self-protection that turns into silence: withdrawing, testing, expecting others to guess. Growth for Cancer is learning that asking directly is safer than it feels.", "growth": "A simple practice for Cancer: when hurt, say 'that stung' before retreating. In relationships, Cancer does well to let people earn trust in small steps instead of all at once or not at all.", "tarot": "In tarot, Cancer is traditionally linked to The Chariot, the card of directed will beneath a guarded shell. The pairing fits: soft inside, determined outside, always moving toward what protects the people they love."}, {"n": "leo", "dates": "Jul 23 - Aug 22", "el": "Fire", "mod": "Fixed", "ruler": "Sun", "traits": "warm, proud, generous, dramatic", "love": "Leo loves loudly and loyally. Appreciation and attention keep the flame going.", "work": "Natural leaders who shine on stage and need recognition.", "card": "Strength", "cardSlug": "strength", "strengths": "Leo energy warms rooms. Generosity, loyalty and the courage to be seen make Leo the person who celebrates others loudly and leads without being asked. The blind spot is the need for applause: fishing, sulking when unthanked, or performing instead of resting. Growth for Leo is learning that worth does not need an audience.", "growth": "A simple practice for Leo: do one generous thing a week that nobody finds out about. In relationships, Leo does well to ask how a partner wants to be loved instead of assuming the grand gesture lands.", "tarot": "In tarot, Leo is traditionally linked to Strength, the card of calm courage and gentle self-mastery. The pairing reframes Leo power: not the roar, but the steady hand."}, {"n": "virgo", "dates": "Aug 23 - Sep 22", "el": "Earth", "mod": "Mutable", "ruler": "Mercury", "traits": "precise, practical, modest, critical", "love": "Virgo shows love through acts of service and quiet detail. Trust builds step by step.", "work": "Analysts and fixers who value quality, health and useful systems.", "card": "The Hermit", "cardSlug": "the-hermit", "strengths": "Virgo energy notices. Precision, usefulness and quiet competence make Virgo the person who fixes what everyone else stepped around. The blind spot is the inner critic: standards so high they turn on the self, and help that lands as correction. Growth for Virgo is learning that done kindly beats done perfectly.", "growth": "A simple practice for Virgo: once a day, let one small thing stay imperfect on purpose. In relationships, Virgo does well to offer help as a question, not a fix.", "tarot": "In tarot, Virgo is traditionally linked to The Hermit, the card of study, craft and inner light. The pairing honors Virgo's real gift: careful attention, carried quietly."}, {"n": "libra", "dates": "Sep 23 - Oct 22", "el": "Air", "mod": "Cardinal", "ruler": "Venus", "traits": "charming, fair, social, indecisive", "love": "Libra is devoted to partnership. Harmony and shared beauty matter, but so does being honest about conflict.", "work": "Diplomats who do well in design, law, mediation and teamwork.", "card": "Justice", "cardSlug": "justice", "strengths": "Libra energy balances. Taste, fairness and social intelligence make Libra the person who can hold two sides of an argument without flinching. The blind spot is the cost: decisions postponed to keep the peace, and a self edited down to fit the room. Growth for Libra is learning that an honest no keeps more peace than a resentful yes.", "growth": "A simple practice for Libra: make one small decision a day in under a minute and stand by it. In relationships, Libra does well to state a preference before asking for one.", "tarot": "In tarot, Libra is traditionally linked to Justice, the card of balance, truth and fair consequence. The pairing reflects Libra's deepest wish: a world where things even out."}, {"n": "scorpio", "dates": "Oct 23 - Nov 21", "el": "Water", "mod": "Fixed", "ruler": "Pluto and Mars", "traits": "intense, private, loyal, magnetic", "love": "Scorpio loves deeply and all in. Trust is earned slowly and betrayal is rarely forgotten.", "work": "Researchers and strategists who thrive on depth and transformation.", "card": "Death", "cardSlug": "death", "strengths": "Scorpio energy goes deep. Focus, loyalty and emotional X-ray vision make Scorpio the friend people tell their real secrets to. The blind spot is control: testing loyalty, holding grudges, and treating vulnerability as a risk instead of a bridge. Growth for Scorpio is learning that trust, once given, is stronger than surveillance.", "growth": "A simple practice for Scorpio: share one small true thing before asking for one. In relationships, Scorpio does well to say 'I am hurt' instead of reaching for the sting.", "tarot": "In tarot, Scorpio is traditionally linked to Death, the card of endings that turn into transformation. The pairing fits Scorpio's real nature: not darkness, but the courage to let old skins fall away."}, {"n": "sagittarius", "dates": "Nov 22 - Dec 21", "el": "Fire", "mod": "Mutable", "ruler": "Jupiter", "traits": "free, honest, optimistic, restless", "love": "Sagittarius needs a partner who is also a friend and adventure companion. Freedom is not the enemy of love for them.", "work": "Explorers who do well with travel, teaching, big ideas and variety.", "card": "Temperance", "cardSlug": "temperance", "strengths": "Sagittarius energy expands. Optimism, honesty and appetite for the wide world make Sagittarius the person who makes everyone else's plans feel bigger. The blind spot is restlessness: promises made loosely, tact skipped, and leaving before the harvest. Growth for Sagittarius is learning that freedom and follow-through can share a calendar.", "growth": "A simple practice for Sagittarius: before saying yes, check the calendar and the energy budget, then answer. In relationships, Sagittarius does well to deliver honesty with a soft edge.", "tarot": "In tarot, Sagittarius is traditionally linked to Temperance, the card of alchemy, patience and the middle path. The pairing is a gentle joke the tradition plays: the wildest sign gets the card of blending and balance."}, {"n": "capricorn", "dates": "Dec 22 - Jan 19", "el": "Earth", "mod": "Cardinal", "ruler": "Saturn", "traits": "disciplined, ambitious, reserved, dependable", "love": "Capricorn takes love seriously and shows it by showing up for years, not days.", "work": "Planners who climb steadily and are built for long-term goals.", "card": "The Devil", "cardSlug": "the-devil", "strengths": "Capricorn energy endures. Discipline, dry humor and long-range patience make Capricorn the person who is still standing, and still building, years later. The blind spot is the weight: work becoming identity, feelings filed as unproductive, and rest treated as something to earn. Growth for Capricorn is learning that a life is also a result.", "growth": "A simple practice for Capricorn: schedule rest like a meeting and keep the appointment. In relationships, Capricorn does well to share the plan and the feeling, not only the plan.", "tarot": "In tarot, Capricorn is traditionally linked to The Devil, the card of bondage to what we build. The pairing is a warning and a gift: Capricorn sees the chains, and can choose which ones to keep."}, {"n": "aquarius", "dates": "Jan 20 - Feb 18", "el": "Air", "mod": "Fixed", "ruler": "Saturn and Uranus", "traits": "original, independent, humane, aloof", "love": "Aquarius loves minds and values. Friendship first, with space to be themselves.", "work": "Innovators who thrive in tech, causes and unconventional paths.", "card": "The Star", "cardSlug": "the-star", "strengths": "Aquarius energy rethinks. Originality, principle and genuine care for the collective make Aquarius the person asking why the room accepts what it accepts. The blind spot is distance: living in ideas, intellectualizing feelings, and being everywhere except right here. Growth for Aquarius is learning that presence is also a radical act.", "growth": "A simple practice for Aquarius: once a day, name a feeling before an opinion. In relationships, Aquarius does well to say 'I am here' with actions at small scale, not only ideals at large scale.", "tarot": "In tarot, Aquarius is traditionally linked to The Star, the card of hope, renewal and pouring out for others. The pairing fits the water-bearer exactly: hope carried for everyone."}, {"n": "pisces", "dates": "Feb 19 - Mar 20", "el": "Water", "mod": "Mutable", "ruler": "Neptune and Jupiter", "traits": "dreamy, empathic, artistic, escapist", "love": "Pisces loves with imagination and compassion. Clear boundaries help them stay grounded.", "work": "Creatives and healers who need meaning in their work.", "card": "The Moon", "cardSlug": "the-moon", "strengths": "Pisces energy feels the room before anyone speaks. Imagination, compassion and artistic instinct make Pisces the person who understands what you meant, not what you said. The blind spot is porousness: absorbing everyone else's moods, escaping into daydream, and boundaries drawn in pencil. Growth for Pisces is learning that a boundary is a kindness, not a wall.", "growth": "A simple practice for Pisces: once a day, ask 'is this feeling mine?' before carrying it. In relationships, Pisces does well to say what they need in plain words, even when the other person 'should know'.", "tarot": "In tarot, Pisces is traditionally linked to The Moon, the card of intuition, dreams and tides. The pairing honors Pisces' real terrain: the half-lit places where feelings are truer than facts."}];
